WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.070
Forget that the comic books ever existed.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:06.940
In the movies of the MCU, there's still so
much about the relationship between the Hulk

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.090
and Black Widow that's just plain strange.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:14.410
Let's take a long, unblinking look at all
the bizarre elements about the Hulk and Black

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.880
Widow's relationship.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:21.430
With the 2015 film Avengers: Age of Ultron,
writer and director Joss Whedon surprised

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:26.430
fans by pairing Natasha Romanoff otherwise
known as Black Widow with Bruce Banner, who

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.390
transforms into the Hulk.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:32.340
Their relationship hasn't gone too far in
the films… at least, not yet.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.220
Murderous rampages brought on by psychic assaults
and epic battles with armies of robots always

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.399
get in the way.

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:39.840
Because they always do.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.491
The romance wasn't something anyone could've
predicted, at least not before Avengers: Age

00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:46.940
of Ultron went into full swing.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.190
That's when viewers began to take a real interest
in those scenes featuring Black Widow touching

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:54.219
hands with Bruce Banner's more monstrous half.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:57.329
The story has no equivalent in the pages of
the comics.

00:00:57.329 --> 00:01:01.310
Bruce Banner and Natasha Romanoff barely have
any connection with one another in the source

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:05.339
material, other than the fact that they've
both been members of the Avengers.

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:08.480
But the movies tell a very different story,
don't they?

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.560
The first onscreen meeting between Bruce Banner
and Natasha Romanoff certainly doesn't look

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.399
like love at first sight.

00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:19.360
At the beginning of The Avengers, Black Widow
is abruptly pulled off an assignment in Russia

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.960
to recruit Bruce Banner to help find the stolen
Tesseract.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.160
SHIELD evidently knew Banner was in Calcutta,
and managed to track him down.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.640
Romanoff hires a little girl to lure Banner
to a shack outside of the city, under the

00:01:31.649 --> 00:01:34.320
false pretense that her father is sick.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.780
Once Black Widow's trap is revealed, she uses
her sex appeal and lies to draw Banner closer.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.529
She tells him there's no one outside waiting
for him, and that Nick Fury's interest in

00:01:43.529 --> 00:01:46.029
him has nothing to do with "The Other Guy."

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.280
You know the one.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.600
[Hulk smashing.]

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.119
Smelling a rat, Banner purposely frightens
Romanoff, getting enraged so that she reveals

00:01:56.119 --> 00:01:57.140
her true intentions.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:59.070
"Nobody's gonna put you-"

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.009
"Stop lying to me!"

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.750
That's when Black Widow contacts all those
supposedly nonexistent SHIELD soldiers, with

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.549
all their high-tech weaponry.

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:13.050
Of course, these aren't exactly the solid
foundations of a nurturing, long-lasting relationship.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.580
And can we talk about the fact that Black
Widow felt the need to lure Banner into a

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:17.610
shack?

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.469
And so she hired a little girl to shamelessly
lie?

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:24.060
To a guy who turns into a giant green monster
when he's upset?

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.260
It's all very, very shady.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.960
"That's a dealbreaker!"

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.239
We know it isn't easy to fluster Black Widow,
because she's a master at keeping her cool

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:33.380
in dangerous situations.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:37.980
In fact, the only time we've ever really seen
her go off the deep end was during her first

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.530
encounter with an enraged Hulk in The Avengers.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:45.420
When Bruce Banner turns into the Hulk aboard
SHIELD's Helicarrier, we catch a glimpse of

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.610
Joss Whedon's directing prowess when it comes
to horror.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:52.909
Romanoff hides from the Hulk in the bowels
of the ship, but once he finds her, she doesn't

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.400
stand a chance.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.320
[HUUUUUUUUUUUUULK]

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.859
In one of the most memorable scenes in The
Avengers, the Hulk crashes through the Helicarrier

00:03:02.859 --> 00:03:08.040
in hot pursuit of Black Widow, eventually
backhanding her into a wall before being interrupted

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.200
by Thor.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.290
Afterwards, we see Black Widow is quite shaken.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.030
Even though the battle is continuing throughout
the Helicarrier, she's sitting in the corner

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:19.180
and clearly recovering from the terrifying
encounter.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:22.359
It's the only time we've seen her like this
in any of the films.

00:03:22.359 --> 00:03:26.760
It seems a little crazy that the very same
man who inspired this trauma - in a team full

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:32.120
of handsome and mostly single men - should
be the one that she's drawn to the most...

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.440
In case you didn't know, the Hulk and Banner
don't like each other very much.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:39.950
They don't consider each other the same person,
and they really don't like it when they're

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:42.519
praised for the qualities of the other.

00:03:42.519 --> 00:03:46.790
There are plenty of instances where the Hulk
seems resentful or even jealous of Banner,

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:47.920
and vice versa.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.260
"You're Banner's friend."

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.840
"I'm not Banner's friend, I… prefer you."

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.189
"Banner's friend!"

00:03:53.189 --> 00:03:57.060
And when you think about that, a victorious
scene in Avengers: Age of Ultron seems to

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.239
take on a much darker tone.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:03.489
When Banner frees Black Widow from Ultron's
prison and suggests that they run and go into

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:06.440
hiding, she lures him in for a kiss and says:

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.680
"I adore you."

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.240
"But I need the Other Guy."

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:20.640
Stop to think about the negative feelings
Banner and the Hulk have for one another.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.419
Consider the emotional and physical torture
he goes through when he's transforming.

00:04:24.419 --> 00:04:29.370
The fact becomes clear: What Black Widow did
here was pretty bad, at least as far as potential

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.060
girlfriends are concerned!

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.560
After all, she's seen Banner painfully morph
into the Hulk herself.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.160
Let's just say this incident would be high
on the list of issues for the two to work

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.160
out in couples therapy.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.320
Black Widow is a professional assassin, and
an expert at hiding in plain sight.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:49.410
In Captain America: The Winter Soldier, she
knew how to get trained professional soldiers

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.580
off her scent with only a moment's warning.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:56.860
In fact, these kinds of evasive tactics are
like second nature to the former Soviet agent.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.550
If you're ever on the run and suddenly need
to get right off the grid, Natasha Romanoff

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.520
would be a very good friend to have.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.590
But Bruce Banner?

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.250
Well, not so much.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:09.060
In the wake of the Hulk's rampage, Banner
knows he'll have to go back on the run.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.610
And when he tells Black Widow he has to go,
she responds:

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:14.430
"But you assume that I have to stay?"

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.650
But if you think about it, how could Romanoff
even consider going on the run with Bruce

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:19.650
Banner?

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.979
In order for their love affair to work, they'd
have to hide themselves and remain hidden,

00:05:22.979 --> 00:05:26.700
while remaining ready to drop everything and
run at a moment's notice.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.199
Could Black Widow live that way?

00:05:28.199 --> 00:05:29.199
Sure.

00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:31.370
But how could she live that way with Bruce
Banner?

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.729
They'd need to keep a low profile.

00:05:32.729 --> 00:05:35.949
They'd also need to go unnoticed and keep
their cool.

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:39.550
How can a guy who changes into a giant green
monster whenever he can't find the remote

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.050
ever be trusted to keep a low profile?

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:43.430
And how could he go unnoticed?

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:48.500
Really, how could Bruce Banner ever be anything
to Natasha Romanoff but a cinder block chained

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.480
to her ankle?

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:55.120
At the end of Avengers: Age of Ultron, Romanoff
asks Nick Fury if he foresaw the romance that

00:05:55.139 --> 00:05:57.259
developed between she and Banner.

00:05:57.259 --> 00:06:01.539
His answer is a little vague, but he implies
he saw the potential, telling her:

00:06:01.539 --> 00:06:04.110
"You never know.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.229
You hope for the best.

00:06:05.229 --> 00:06:07.550
And make do with what you get."

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:12.599
So what did Nick Fury see in Banner and Romanoff
that made him think they'd be a good match?

00:06:12.599 --> 00:06:16.729
Was it a simple matter of that old cliché
about how "opposites attract?"

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:19.720
Perhaps more importantly, why did he decide
to act on it?

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.430
How would Fury benefit from Banner and Romanoff
being in a romantic relationship?

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:26.570
Does he think it might help keep Banner in
the fold?

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:31.030
Does he hope Romanoff will be a failsafe - an
easy way to take out Banner if he needs to?

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.259
We may never know.

00:06:32.259 --> 00:06:33.919
But we know he did it for a reason.

00:06:33.919 --> 00:06:36.449
Nick Fury is a calculating man, after all.

00:06:36.449 --> 00:06:41.039
Plus, manipulating a master assassin and a
man who occasionally turns into a green monster

00:06:41.039 --> 00:06:43.970
is inherently dangerous business, obviously.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.440
He wouldn't have done it if he didn't think
it was important.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.720
We doubt he really enjoys playing matchmaker.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:54.639
The Hulk has a penchant for scattering crowds
of scared soldiers, dodging missiles, and

00:06:54.639 --> 00:06:56.289
tearing through airplanes.

00:06:56.289 --> 00:07:02.169
Meanwhile, Black Widow is a former agent of
SHIELD, which is an outgrowth of the US military...an

00:07:02.169 --> 00:07:05.870
organization that's never taken too kindly
to the Hulk's antics.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.740
That's why when she appears in that shack
in The Avengers, Banner knows exactly the

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.650
kind of person he's dealing with.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.630
He's dealt with the likes of her before.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:17.030
And really, that makes his feelings for her
even more strange.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:21.810
By the time Avengers: Age of Ultron opens,
Banner has won some trust with the world at

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.819
large… but he knows how quickly that can
change.

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:26.159
And it does change.

00:07:26.159 --> 00:07:29.830
Were their relationship to go any further,
Romanoff might one day be put in the position

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:33.199
of having to assassinate Banner… or at least
try.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.600
Strange bedfellows indeed!

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.240
When Banner and Betty Ross are hiding out
in a motel in The Incredible Hulk, the close

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.349
quarters and raw emotions mean things get
hot and heavy real quick.

00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:48.500
Oh, and Edward Norton plays the Hulk in that
film, in case you're wondering whether Banner

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:51.680
just underwent another remarkable transformation.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.900
Luckily for Ross and every other guest at
the motel, Banner's wearing a heart monitor

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:58.490
on his wrist when they start making out.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:03.020
Before things go too far, Banner cuts things
off because his heart monitor starts beeping.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:07.990
"Wait, wait, wait, we can't do this."

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:11.699
Getting physical with Ross, he soon learns,
doesn't seem to be an option when he's sharing

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:12.880
a body with the Hulk.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.139
Of course, it's possible that all that has
changed.

00:08:16.139 --> 00:08:20.379
As we saw at the end of The Incredible Hulk
and the end of The Avengers, Banner has more

00:08:20.379 --> 00:08:23.240
control over his transformation than he used
to.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.569
But that control is still rather shaky.

00:08:25.569 --> 00:08:27.479
We saw him change in Avengers.

00:08:27.479 --> 00:08:31.670
We also saw him change during Scarlet Witch's
psychic assault in Age of Ultron.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:36.110
And in Thor: Ragnarok, we learned Banner had
no control when he became the Hulk and stayed

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.560
the Hulk for two whole years.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:41.710
In fact, he apparently doesn't even remember
any of it.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:46.560
Considering all that, how could Black Widow
ever consider risking her heart and her life?

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:49.450
Of course, on the other hand, Mark Ruffalo
is pretty dreamy...

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.980
Why did the Hulk decide to leave at the end
of Age of Ultron?

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:57.220
Of course, there were plenty of reasons for
him to go.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:01.750
At the time, it seemed like a rather selfless
move, but the events of Thor: Ragnarok really

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:04.140
shine a new light on his actions.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:08.500
We know for a fact that the Hulk never changed
back into Banner for two years after the events

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:10.060
in Age of Ultron.

00:09:10.060 --> 00:09:13.470
We also know Banner wasn't in control for
most of that time.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:17.530
Banner tells Thor that, in the past, he felt
like both he and the Hulk had some control

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:18.910
over their actions.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:23.160
But for the two years between Age of Ultron
and Ragnarok, Banner claims the Hulk was in

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.760
sole control of his body:

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:28.960
"I mean, in the past, I always felt like Hulk
and I each had a hand on the wheel, but this

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:32.600
time it's like he had the keys to the car
and I was locked in the trunk."

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:37.440
If that's true, it wasn't Banner's choice
to leave Romanoff, the Avengers, and Earth.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.510
It was the Hulk's choice.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:43.660
And if that's the case, it seems clear he
did it so he could remain the Hulk indefinitely.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:47.520
We know Black Widow has figured out a way
to "lullabye" Hulk back into Banner.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:51.160
And we know it was the video recording of
Black Widow that triggered Hulk to finally

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.160
change back to Banner in Ragnarok.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.960
"Nice work, big guy.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.870
We don't know where Ulton is headed but you're
going very high, very fast, so…"

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:00.640
So here's a theory for you.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:04.721
Even though Natasha is the one who pushed
Banner down the hole to summon the Hulk, perhaps

00:10:04.721 --> 00:10:09.120
the Hulk left Earth not in spite of Natasha,
but because of her.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:12.290
Perhaps he wanted to remain the Hulk because
he didn't want Banner's relationship with

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:13.980
her to put him back to sleep.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:17.800
Do you think we're onto something here…
or have we gone completely mad?

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.270
[HULKY HULK HULKSTER]

